        }
      ],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Ferrari's stocks plunged after the presentation of the company's first electric car, Luce. The market reacted harshly: the design of the car for $640,000 was compared to Tesla Model 3 and Chinese electric cars. Users blame Jony Ive, the former chief designer at Apple, who was entrusted with the project.\n\nThe paradox is that on paper everything is fine for Ferrari: the revenue for 2025 is record-breaking at €7.1 billion. But investors are concerned about something else - Lamborghini and Porsche have already slowed down on electrification because the demand for such cars is extremely low. However, Ferrari is going against the tide, and apparently, it's a mistake.",
