      "contentType": "text",
      "media": [],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Brazil: who can obtain a digital nomad visa VITEM XI in 2026\n\nVisaHQ has published a detailed analysis of the rules for the Brazilian digital nomad visa (VITEM XI) for the year 2026.\n\nMain requirements:\n- Income from abroad of at least $1,500 per month or savings of $18,000\n- Contract with a foreign employer or clients\n- Certificate of no criminal record for the last 5 years\n- Health insurance valid in Brazil\n\nImportant: If you receive a salary from a Brazilian company, you need to apply for a regular work visa (VITEM V).\n\nHow to apply:\n- At a Brazilian consulate abroad\n- Or through the MigranteWeb portal (if you are already in the country)\n\nProcessing time is up to 120 days. The fee in 2026 is R$ 204.77.\n\nBrazil remains one of the most accessible options among G20 countries in terms of minimum income requirements. The program is particularly convenient for companies launching \"work-from-anywhere\" pilots.",
